{
  "raw": {
    "https://my.corehr.com/pls/shurecruit/erq_jobspec_version_4.jobspec?p_id=120788": {
      "title": "Associate Lecturer Primary Education",
      "description": "Closing Date: 25/10/2026 Associate Lecturer Primary Education College of Social Sciences & Arts Academic Grade 7, £40,704 to £45,641 depending on experience Sheffield Institute of Education (SIoE) offers sector leading initial teacher training in early years, primary, secondary and post-16 and we are rated outstanding in all four areas by Ofsted. We are currently looking for applications for Associate Lecturers for the Primary Education area of our provision with experience and expertise across Key Stage 1 and 2 . The role will be teaching and supporting students on placement across Undergraduate and Postgraduate courses in Early years and Primary with QTS . The role will include responsibility for the teaching, learning and assessment of students at postgraduate level, alongside working collaboratively with our partnership schools to support trainee placement experiences . The post holder will contribute to delivering a high-quality curriculum that supports trainees in developing strong subject knowledge, pedagogical understanding, and reflective practice in primary education. Staff members often teach across our provision. The successful candidate may also be asked to contribute to Secondary Initial Teacher Education (ITE) and School Centered Initial Teacher Training (SCITT) , as well other related teaching at Masters or Undergraduate level , undertaking school visits , and providing academic advising . We encourage staff to continue to develop their own research and scholarly profile , particularly in areas related to primary education, curriculum development, or teacher education. There are a range of opportunities and support mechanisms available to enable all academic staff to engage in research, knowledge exchange, and professional practice. We offer a diverse range of benefits and opportunities to pursue a rewarding and fulfilling career in a supportive environment. The University currently enrols eligible academic staff into the Teachers’ Pension Scheme (TPS), a defined-benefit pension scheme. Further details on TPS can be found here . Sheffield Hallam welcomes applications from all candidates irrespective of age, pregnancy and maternity, disability, sex, gender reassignment, sexual orientation, race, religion or belief, or marital or civil partnership status. For this job we particularly welcome applications from ethnic minority applicants who are underrepresented in this area/this type of job at Sheffield Hallam If you are offered this post you will be subject to an enhanced with barred lists check-child workforce by the Disclosure and Barring Service. A criminal record will not necessarily prevent you from working at Sheffield Hallam University but its relevance to the duties of the post will need to be assessed before the appointment is confirmed. The role is not eligible for sponsorship under the Skilled Worker route so if you are an international applicant, you will need to ensure you have an appropriate visa to evidence the necessary right to work in the UK. For more information, please visit the UKVI Guidance before applying. To find out more, take a look at our guide to applying. We recommend you download the job description and person specification when you apply, as this will not be available once the job has closed. Accessibility We are committed to ensuring our materials are accessible to all. If you encounter any accessibility barriers or have suggestions for improvement please contact us using our web accessibility report form. Your feedback helps us enhance our accessibility efforts and improve our services. Contact Person : Jemma Monkhouse Contact Number : Date Advertised : 12-Oct-2026 Closing Date : 25-Oct-2026 Employment Type : Contact Email : j.monkhouse@shu.ac.uk Job number : 120788"
    },
    "https://my.corehr.com/pls/shurecruit/erq_jobspec_version_4.jobspec?p_id=120567": {
      "title": "CRM Manager",
      "description": "Closing Date: 01/11/2026 CRM Manager Recruitment, Communications & Marketing Professional & Business Support Grade 7 - £40,704 to £45,641 per annum (depending on experience) We have an exciting opportunity to join a fast-paced, collaborative, and supportive Student Recruitment Marketing team, playing a critical role in delivering personalised. targeted student recruitment and marketing activities, as well as providing leadership across a range of business areas to ensure consistent, best practice CRM activity across the full student recruitment journey. You will work primarily in our CRM system (Microsoft Dynamics), to manage the development of complex and dynamic customer journeys which power personalised, targeted marketing activities. You’ll also be responsible for troubleshooting issues and system development for the CRM system and associated technologies and delivering new and innovative ways of working, supporting training and development where required. You'll work with the CRM Data and Insights Manager to ensure high data quality and integrity in our CRM system, collaborating with teams across student recruitment, marketing and Digital Technology Services. You’ll provide expertise and advice to ensure high data standards, GDPR compliance, and support technical enhancements to enhance performance and user experience. You are a CRM specialist with a keen eye for detail and a passion for pushing the boundaries to plan and optimise CRM campaigns to meet business objectives. You’re comfortable working with relational data and complex audience information to create customer journeys and can share knowledge and expertise to develop and implement a CRM strategy across student recruitment that ensures consistency, compliance and high-quality engagements with future students. We are looking for someone with: Extensive CRM experience, ideally with Microsoft Dynamics. A pro-active approach to using and developing new systems and software. An exceptional communicator and collaborator, with the ability to build relationships and demonstrate leadership across functional boundaries. Experience of navigating complex regulatory environments, with strong working knowledge of GDPR. Experience in Higher Education is desirable, along with experience of managing CRM integrations and using data extraction and reporting tools. We offer a diverse range of benefits and opportunities to pursue a rewarding and fulfilling career in a supportive environment. You will be contractually enrolled into the Local Government Pension Scheme (LGPS) one of the largest and most generous defined benefit pension schemes in the country. Find out more about the LGPS. If you are, or have been, a recent member of the Universities Superannuation Scheme (USS) directly prior to joining us, you can choose to opt out of the LGPS and remain in the USS. Please contact the Pensions team to discuss options available. Sheffield Hallam welcomes applications from all candidates irrespective of age, pregnancy and maternity, disability, sex, gender reassignment, sexual orientation, race, religion or belief, or marital or civil partnership status. For this job we particularly welcome applications from ethnic minority applicants who are underrepresented in this area/this type of job at Sheffield Hallam. The role is not likely to be eligible for sponsorship under the Skilled Worker route so if you are an international applicant, you will need to ensure you have an appropriate visa to evidence the necessary right to work in the UK. For more information, please visit the UKVI Guidance before applying. We welcome applications for job-share, part-time and flexible working arrangements. To find out more, take a look at our guide to applying. We recommend you download the job description and person specification when you apply, as this will not be available once the job has closed. Accessibility We are committed to ensuring our materials are accessible to all. If you encounter any accessibility barriers or have suggestions for improvement please contact us using our web accessibility report form . Your feedback helps us enhance our accessibility efforts and improve our services. Contact Person : Sarah Jenkins Contact Number : Date Advertised : 08-Oct-2026 Closing Date : 01-Nov-2026 Location : Level 2, Furnival Works Employment Type : Permanent - Full Time Job number : 120567 Contact Email : s.e.jenkins@shu.ac.uk"
    },
    "https://my.corehr.com/pls/shurecruit/erq_jobspec_version_4.jobspec?p_id=120387": {
      "title": "Executive Director of Human Resources and Organisational Development",
      "description": "Closing Date: 19/10/2026 Executive Director of Human Resources and Organisational Development Human Resources & Org Development Other Competitive salary Sheffield Hallam University is seeking an outstanding people leader to shape its workforce, culture and organisational capability during an important period in its development. Sheffield Hallam is one of the UK’s largest and most diverse universities, with around 31,000 students, 3,700 colleagues and more than 330,000 alumni. Its purpose is simple: to transform lives. Through applied education, research and partnerships, the University addresses real-world challenges and makes a significant contribution to Sheffield, South Yorkshire and beyond. Reporting to the Chief Operating Officer and working closely with the Vice-Chancellor, the Executive Director of Human Resources and Organisational Development will be a member of the University Executive Board. They will lead the University’s people agenda and contribute fully to institution-wide strategy, planning and decision-making, ensuring that people considerations are central to the choices Sheffield Hallam makes. The Executive Director will lead the HR and Organisational Development Directorate, encompassing workforce strategy and planning, organisational development, employee and industrial relations, resourcing and reward, people policy, payroll, pensions and HR administration. They will continue to develop an effective and trusted service, closely connected to the University’s academic and operational priorities. A central focus will be shaping Sheffield Hallam’s future workforce strategy and strengthening organisational design, leadership capability, career development and performance. The successful candidate will also lead the University’s approach to employee relations, building constructive relationships with recognised trade unions and supporting the institution through continuing change. Candidates will bring substantial senior HR leadership experience gained in a large, complex and unionised organisation. They will have led people strategy, organisational change and the delivery of high-quality HR and organisational development services. Strong experience of employee relations, workforce transformation and advising at executive and Board level will be essential. Sheffield Hallam welcomes candidates from other complex organisations who can build trust, influence across professional boundaries and connect people strategy with organisational performance and financial sustainability. This is an opportunity to join a university with a strong public purpose, a distinctive place in its region and clear ambition for the future. Sheffield Hallam is looking for a visible, thoughtful and collaborative leader who will listen carefully and provide confidence and direction for its next phase. Full details and applications can be made at https://candidate.andersonquigley.com/Sheffield-Hallam-University-Executive-Director-of-HR-and-OD . The closing date for applications is noon, Monday 19 October 2026. For this job, we particularly welcome applications from minority ethnic applicants who are underrepresented in this type of role at Sheffield Hallam. Contact Person : Anderson Quigley Contact Email : Date Advertised : 24-Sep-2026 Closing Date : 19-Oct-2026 Contact Number : Job number : 120387"
    },
    "https://my.corehr.com/pls/shurecruit/erq_jobspec_version_4.jobspec?p_id=120027": {
      "title": "Lecturer in Chemistry",
      "description": "Closing Date: 18/10/2026 Lecturer in Chemistry College of Health Wellbeing&Life Science Academic Grade 7 - £39,906 to £44,746 per annum (depending on experience) Here at Sheffield Hallam University we are seeking a Lecturer in Chemistry to join our Chemistry team on a 12-month fixed term contract. The successful candidate will contribute to the delivery of high-quality teaching across our undergraduate and postgraduate chemistry provision, with a particular focus on chemistry, including lectures, laboratory teaching, assessment and supervision of student projects. Applicants should have a strong academic background in chemistry or a closely related discipline, with current knowledge of the practical and theoretical aspects of chemistry. The University has invested significantly in new laboratory equipment for teaching and research in recent years. Our chemistry facilities have been further enhanced following the award of £5m from the Higher Education Funding Council for England (HEFCE) match-funded by the University, to create new facilities for STEM (science, technology, engineering and mathematics) provision, including an additional chemistry laboratory and a publicly accessible environment as a resource for nurturing enterprising, work-ready students. We offer a diverse range of benefits and opportunities to pursue a rewarding and fulfilling career in a supportive environment. The University currently enrols eligible academic staff into the Teachers’ Pension Scheme (TPS), a defined-benefit pension scheme. Further details on TPS can be found here. Sheffield Hallam welcomes applications from all candidates irrespective of age, pregnancy and maternity, disability, sex, gender reassignment, sexual orientation, race, religion or belief, or marital or civil partnership status. For this job we particularly welcome applications from ethnic minority applicants who are underrepresented in this area/this type of job at Sheffield Hallam. The University may be able to sponsor the employment of international applicants in this role; this will depend on a number of factors specific to the individual applicant. You are advised to assess your eligibility against the criteria set out in the UKVI Guidance before applying. We welcome applications for job-share, part-time and flexible working arrangements. To find out more, take a look at our guide to applying . We recommend you download the job description and person specification when you apply, as this will not be available once the job has closed. Accessibility We are committed to ensuring our materials are accessible to all. If you encounter any accessibility barriers or have suggestions for improvement please contact us using our web accessibility report form . Your feedback helps us enhance our accessibility efforts and improve our services. Contact Person : Dr Laura Cole Contact Number : Date Advertised : 24-Sep-2026 Closing Date : 18-Oct-2026 Employment Type : Fixed Term - Full Time Location : City, Howard Street Contact Email : l.cole@shu.ac.uk Job number : 120027"
    },
    "https://my.corehr.com/pls/shurecruit/erq_jobspec_version_4.jobspec?p_id=120287": {
      "title": "Lecturer in Occupational Therapy",
      "description": "Closing Date: 25/10/2026 Lecturer in Occupational Therapy College of Health Wellbeing&Life Science Academic Grade 7 - £39,906 to £44,746 per annum (pro rata) depending on experience Are you an experienced Occupational Therapist looking for a new challenge? If you're a Band 6, or an experienced Band 5 ready to take the next step, this is your opportunity to shape the future generation of the profession whilst developing your own academic career. We're looking for an enthusiastic HCPC-registered Occupational Therapist with expertise in teaching, training and supervision to join our supportive and ambitious team within the School of Health and Social Care. As one of the UK's leading providers of allied health education, we deliver a diverse portfolio of undergraduate, postgraduate and degree apprenticeship programmes across 14 registered professions. As part of our team, you'll play a pivotal role in teaching, assessment and academic activities contributing to our BSc (Hons) Occupational Therapy Degree Apprenticeship and cross teaching to our full-time BSc Hons Occupational Therapy programme, helping to prepare competent, compassionate and practice-ready graduates. This is an exciting opportunity to inspire students from a wide range of backgrounds through innovative teaching, assessment and research. You'll work closely with the course team and practice partners to ensure our programmes reflect the realities of contemporary occupational therapy practice and the changing needs of the NHS/other sectors. Whether your experience comes from pioneering new models of care in primary or secondary care, leading service innovation, or supporting pre-registration learners, you'll bring valuable insight that enriches the student experience. We'll support your own professional development. You'll have opportunities to build your academic profile, develop your research interests, and, where appropriate, gain a Postgraduate Certificate in Teaching in Higher Education. If you're passionate about developing the next generation of dietitians and want to combine your clinical expertise with a rewarding career in higher education, we'd love to hear from you. Come and meet us! If you have any questions or would like to meet our friendly team before applying, you're warmly invited to attend our Open Event on Tuesday 13th October 2026 at 16:00hrs. To book your place, please contact Katie Peck Associate Head of School – Professional Lead (Occupational Therapy and Dietetics) at email: k.peck@shu.ac.uk We offer a diverse range of benefits and opportunities to pursue a rewarding and fulfilling career in a supportive environment. The University currently enrols eligible academic staff into the Teachers’ Pension Scheme (TPS), a defined-benefit pension scheme. Further details on TPS can be found here . If you’re a member of the Universities Superannuation Scheme (USS) directly before joining us, you can choose to remain in USS instead. Sheffield Hallam welcomes applications from all candidates irrespective of age, pregnancy and maternity, disability, sex, gender reassignment, sexual orientation, race, religion or belief, or marital or civil partnership status. For this job we particularly welcome applications from ethnic minority applicants who are underrepresented in this area/this type of job at Sheffield Hallam. The role is not likely to be eligible for sponsorship under the Skilled Worker route so if you are an international applicant, you will need to ensure you have an appropriate visa to evidence the necessary right to work in the UK. For more information, please visit the UKVI Guidance before applying. We welcome applications for job-share, and flexible working arrangements. To find out more, take a look at our guide to applying. We recommend you download the job description and person specification when you apply, as this will not be available once the job has closed. Accessibility We are committed to ensuring our materials are accessible to all. If you encounter any accessibility barriers or have suggestions for improvement, please contact us using our web accessibility report form . Your feedback helps us enhance our accessibility efforts and improve our services. Contact Person : Katie Peck Contact Number : Date Advertised : 25-Sep-2026 Closing Date : 25-Oct-2026 Employment Type : Permanent - Part Time Location : Collegiate Campus Contact Email : k.peck@shu.ac.uk Job number : 120287"
    },
    "https://my.corehr.com/pls/shurecruit/erq_jobspec_version_4.jobspec?p_id=120047": {
      "title": "Lecturer in Quantity Surveying",
      "description": "Closing Date: 18/10/2026 Lecturer in Quantity Surveying College of Business, Tech. & Engineering Academic £39,906 to £44,746 dependent on experience Do you fancy a change in career? Are you looking to redress the work-life balance? Inspire the next generation of Quantity Surveyors by joining our team! The School of Engineering and Built Environment is one of the UK's leading providers of post and undergraduate education in the fields of Construction and Surveying. Our courses in this area are very well regarded by students and employers alike. We are looking for an inspirational Lecturer with a commitment to the enhancement of our curriculum, teaching and student experience to join our successful Quantity Surveying team. You will be expected to undertake teaching and administrative duties on our undergraduate, postgraduate and business to business programmes using your practical experience to inspire students. For this post there will be opportunities to contribute into areas of the curriculum, including Measurement (essential), Cost planning/ Commercial Management, Digital Construction, Procurement, Sustainable Construction and Contract Administration for the successful candidate. We offer a diverse range of benefits and opportunities to pursue a rewarding and fulfilling career in a supportive environment. Sheffield Hallam welcomes applications from all candidates irrespective of age, pregnancy and maternity, disability, sex, gender reassignment, sexual orientation, race, religion or belief, or marital or civil partnership status. We welcome applications for job-share, part-time and flexible working arrangements. To find out more, take a look at our guide to applying. We recommend you download the job description and person specification when you apply, as this will not be available once the job has closed. Accessibility We are committed to ensuring our materials are accessible to all. If you encounter any accessibility barriers or have suggestions for improvement please contact us using our web accessibility report form . Your feedback helps us enhance our accessibility efforts and improve our services. Contact Person : Collette King Contact Number : Date Advertised : 02-Oct-2026 Closing Date : 18-Oct-2026 Employment Type : Permanent - Full Time Location : City Campus Contact Email : c.king@shu.ac.uk Job number : 120047"
    },
    "https://my.corehr.com/pls/shurecruit/erq_jobspec_version_4.jobspec?p_id=119967": {
      "title": "Lecturer in Systems Engineering",
      "description": "Closing Date: 18/10/2026 Lecturer in Systems Engineering College of Business, Tech. & Engineering Academic Grade 7 - £39,906 to £44,746 per annum (depending on experience) The School of Engineering and Built Environment, part of the College of Business, Technology and Engineering, is home to a vibrant community of academics, researchers, and industry professionals across a wide range of engineering disciplines. We are passionate about developing the next generation of engineering talent and are seeking an inspiring and enthusiastic individual to join our team. Applicants should have practical experience in Knowledge of Systems Engineering, complex electro/mechanical subsystems and integration and its practical application to physical systems. PG Qual or relevant industrial experience in a Systems Engineering related discipline with awareness of current national and international industry developments. This is an exciting opportunity to play a key role in shaping the future workforce within one of the fastest-growing and most innovative sectors of engineering. We welcome applications from candidates with practical, industry-based experience in: Control and automation across multi disciplinary areas such as Mechanical and Aerospace engineering. Whether you are currently working in industry and looking to share your expertise, or an experienced educator seeking a new challenge, we would love to hear from you. Applicants should have an understanding of current and emerging trends within systems engineering , together with an awareness of the opportunities and challenges facing the sector both nationally and internationally. During the selection process, candidates will be invited to demonstrate how their professional knowledge and experience can be applied to inspire and develop future engineers. No Previous Teaching Experience? No Problem. We recognise that some of the most impactful educators begin their careers in industry. If you have practical experience and a passion for developing others, we will support you in making the transition into higher education. This role offers an excellent opportunity to inspire the next generation of engineers while continuing to develop your own professional and academic career. Equally, we welcome applications from existing lecturers and trainers who are passionate about delivering engaging, industry-relevant teaching and helping students realise their career ambitions. Our Engineering Community You will join a collaborative and supportive team that works closely with colleagues across the Power, Electrical and Control Engineering subject area. Together, we deliver a portfolio of highly regarded programmes, including: • CEng-accredited BEng/MEng Electrical and Electronic Engineering • BEng Electrical Engineering (Top-Up) • BEng Mechatronics • MSc Electrical and Electronic Engineering • Degree Apprenticeship Programmes • A broad range of MSc Engineering programmes • Our expertise spans a diverse range of engineering specialisms, including: • Robotics and Automation • Embedded Systems and Microprocessor Engineering • Analogue and Digital Electronics • Computer and Network Engineering • Communications Systems • Systems Simulation and Modelling Make an Impact This is more than a teaching role. It is an opportunity to shape the skills, ambitions and careers of future engineers while contributing to a dynamic and growing engineering community with strong industry links and a commitment to innovation. If you are passionate about robotics, eager to share your expertise, and motivated by the opportunity to influence the engineers of tomorrow, we encourage you to apply. The School The School of Engineering and Built Environment is arranged into a number of subject areas: Electrical, Electronic and Future Technologies, Mechanical Engineering, Future Transportation, Built Environment, and Energy, Infrastructure and Environment. We place equal emphasis on teaching and research, be it subject or pedagogic research into teaching Engineering, Physics and Built Environment to transform lives. With excellent links to industry, we develop innovative products to improve the quality of lives, support the sustainable development of business and provide insights into fundamental questions about our universe. Through our strong industry partners, we provide applied learning opportunities for our students and our graduates perform really well in the labour market. Research, Innovation and Knowledge Exchange in the School has strong alignment with UKRI priority areas, such as Manufacturing the Future, Clean Technologies, AI and Robotics, as well as Digital Innovations for Health. We are a welcoming community where staff and students are encouraged to develop their careers and make a fulfilling impact. We offer a diverse range of benefits and opportunities to pursue a rewarding and fulfilling career in a supportive environment. The University currently enrols eligible academic staff into the Teachers’ Pension Scheme (TPS), a defined-benefit pension scheme. Further details on TPS can be found here. If you’re a member of the Universities Superannuation Scheme (USS) directly before joining us, you can choose to remain in USS instead. Sheffield Hallam welcomes applications from all candidates irrespective of age, pregnancy and maternity, disability, sex, gender reassignment, sexual orientation, race, religion or belief, or marital or civil partnership status. The University may be able to sponsor the employment of international applicants in this role; this will depend on a number of factors specific to the individual applicant. You are advised to assess your eligibility against the criteria set out in the UKVI Guidance before applying. We welcome applications for job-share, part-time and flexible working arrangements. To find out more, take a look at our guide to applying. We recommend you download the job description and person specification when you apply, as this will not be available once the job has closed. Accessibility We are committed to ensuring our materials are accessible to all. If you encounter any accessibility barriers or have suggestions for improvement please contact us using our web accessibility report form . Your feedback helps us enhance our accessibility efforts and improve our services. Contact Person : Catherine Smith Contact Number : Date Advertised : 02-Oct-2026 Closing Date : 18-Oct-2026 Employment Type : Permanent - Full Time Location : Sheaf Contact Email : catherine.smith@shu.ac.uk Job number : 119967"
    },
    "https://my.corehr.com/pls/shurecruit/erq_jobspec_version_4.jobspec?p_id=120127": {
      "title": "Technical Specialist - Aerospace and Materials Science",
      "description": "Closing Date: 18/10/2026 Technical Specialist - Aerospace and Materials Science Technical Operations & Resource Services Other Grade 6, £32,080 to £38,784 depending on experience Sheffield Hallam University Technical Operations Resources and Services (TORS) are excited to welcome a new Technical Specialist supporting aerospace and material science in our undergraduate engineering laboratories. Based within the smaller Computing, Engineering, Technology and Analysis team you will be responsible for supporting staff and students along with laboratory equipment to facilitate taught activities and project work within labs that supports aerospace and material science. You will be educated to HND or above (or have equivalent level of experience) in a relevant subject and have previous experience in working with wind tunnels and material preparation and testing. You should also be a team worker, well-organised and possess good communication and IT skills. In the aerospace area you would be supporting the use of a subsonic wind tunnel and smaller ones specifically modelling airflow over a wing surface. In the material support area, you would be using equipment to determine the tensile strength, tensile impact strength of engineering materials, along with their Vickers hardness. In addition, having knowledge of the effect of heat treatment on alloys would be advantageous along with experience preparing and polishing metal samples for optical microscope investigations. It is expected that you will provide expertise to other technical teams within TORS and support other laboratories associated with the Engineering area from time to time. Some flexibility towards working hours is also required. You do not need to be an expert across all our aerospace and materials activities; however, you do need a can-do attitude, be adaptable, flexible and enjoy learning new skills. If you are passionate about teamwork and working in a multidisciplinary team, customer service, facilitation of learning and have the experiences we are looking for we look forward to your application. We offer a diverse range of benefits and opportunities to pursue a rewarding and fulfilling career in a supportive environment. You will be contractually enrolled into the Local Government Pension Scheme (LGPS) – one of the largest and most generous defined benefit pension schemes in the country. Find out more about the LGPS For this job we particularly welcome applications from ethnic minority applicants who are underrepresented in this area/ this type of job at Sheffield Hallam. Right to work We are unable to employ anyone who does not have the legal right to work in the UK. If you need sponsorship to undertake this role, please use the UK government’s Visas and immigration pages to check your eligibility before applying so you can apply your personal circumstances. More information for international candidates To find out more, take a look at our guide to applying. Accessibility We are committed to ensuring our materials are accessible to all. If you encounter any accessibility barriers or have suggestions for improvement please contact us using our web accessibility report form . Your feedback helps us enhance our accessibility efforts and improve our services. Contact Person : Misko Abramiuk Contact Number : 0114 225 6823 Date Advertised : 24-Sep-2026 Closing Date : 18-Oct-2026 Location : City Campus Employment Type : Permanent - Full Time Job number : 120127 Contact Email : m.m.abramiuk@shu.ac.uk"
    }
  },
